# Every text file is LF in the repository and LF in the working tree, on
# every platform. Git Bash on Windows otherwise warns "LF will be replaced
# by CRLF" for each file an apply script writes, and a stray CRLF in a
# shell script, systemd unit or sourced config breaks it on guildenstern.
# Binary files are detected automatically by text=auto.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit, for the files where CRLF is an outright failure rather than noise.
*.sh text eol=lf
deploy/deploy.config text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer text eol=lf
